29
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,900
Let's begin with one of the most important parts of workplace communication.

30
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:59,740
Starting a conversation.

31
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:04,860
Right. Imagine you arrive at work in the morning. What do you say to your colleagues?

32
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:08,060
The simplest and most natural phrase is, good morning.

33
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:12,460
Yes, very simple. You can also say, good morning. How are you?

34
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:15,820
Or even more casually, morning. How's everything going?

35
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:20,300
That sounds very natural and professional. Let's give a quick example.

36
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:21,020
Sure.

37
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,780
Good morning. How are you today?

38
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,700
I'm good. Thanks. How about you?

39
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:28,140
I'm doing well. Thank you. Ready for a busy day?

40
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:31,740
Perfect. That's a simple but effective workplace conversation.

41
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:34,460
Now let's move to asking for help.

42
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:37,260
This is something we all need to do at work.

43
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:40,060
Yes, and it's very important to sound polite.

44
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:43,900
One of the best phrases is, could you help me with this?

45
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,860
Or, can you give me a hand with this task?

46
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:50,780
Even more polite would be, would you mind helping me with this?

47
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:53,180
That's a great one. Let's do an example.

48
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:55,020
Hey, do you have a moment?

49
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,300
Sure. What's up?

50
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,820
Would you mind helping me with this report?

51
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:00,180
I'm a bit stuck.

52
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,020
Of course, I'd be happy to help.

53
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:04,740
That sounds very natural and professional.

54
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:07,020
Now, what if someone asks you for help?

55
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,380
How do you respond?

56
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:10,740
You can say, sure, no problem.

57
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,700
Or, of course, I can help.

58
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:16,420
If you're busy, you can say, I'm a bit tied up right now,

59
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:17,980
but I can help you later.

60
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:19,900
That's very polite and honest.

61
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,340
Let's practice that.

62
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,300
Can you help me with this presentation?

63
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:26,260
I'd love to, but I'm a bit busy at the moment.

64
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:28,260
Can we look at it this afternoon?

65
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:30,660
That's perfect workplace communication.

66
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:34,360
Now, let's talk about giving opinions in meetings.

67
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:38,260
This is very important because meetings happen in almost every job.

68
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:40,860
A simple phrase is, I think.

69
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,660
Or, in my opinion.

70
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:47,460
If you want to sound more professional, you can say, from my perspective.

71
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:49,460
Nice. Let's do an example.

72
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:53,260
So, what do you think about this new marketing strategy?

73
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:57,500
From my perspective, it's a good idea, but we need more data to support it.

74
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,700
That sounds very professional.

75
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:02,220
Now, what if you disagree with someone?

76
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:05,300
That's tricky. You need to be polite.

77
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:10,740
Exactly. Instead of saying, you're wrong, you can say, I see your point, but...

78
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:14,300
Or, I understand what you're saying, however...

79
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,300
Let's try it.

80
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:18,420
I think we should increase the budget immediately.

81
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:22,140
I see your point, but I think we should review the numbers first.

82
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:24,440
That's respectful and professional.

83
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,940
Now let's talk about making requests.

84
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:30,440
Yes, this is something you do every day at work.

85
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:33,440
A simple phrase is, can you send me the file?

86
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,840
More polite. Could you please send me the file?

87
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:40,440
Even more formal would be, would you be able to send me the file?

88
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:41,740
Let's practice.

89
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,040
Could you please send me the updated document?

90
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:46,140
Sure, I'll send it right away.

91
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:47,040
Perfect.

92
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:50,040
Now let's move to emails and messages.

93
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:53,640
Yes, communication isn't just spoken, it's written too.

94
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:58,280
A common phrase is, just following up on my previous message.

95
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:01,320
Or, I wanted to check if you had any updates.

96
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,840
Let's do an example.

97
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,800
Hi, just following up on the report I sent yesterday.

98
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,640
Have you had a chance to review it?

99
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,800
Yes, I looked at it this morning.

100
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,000
It looks great.

101
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,880
That's very natural workplace communication.

102
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:16,440
Now let's talk about deadlines.

103
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,040
Very important topic.

104
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,520
You can say, when is the deadline?

105
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:23,560
Or, this needs to be completed by Friday.

106
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:27,800
If you need more time, you can say, could I have an extension?

107
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,920
Let's practice.

108
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:32,520
I'm working on the project, but I might need more time.

109
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:34,920
That's fine. When do you think you can finish it?

110
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,000
I can have it ready by Monday.

111
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,960
Sounds good.

112
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,920
Now, let's talk about giving feedback.

113
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:43,480
Very important in professional environments.

114
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:47,560
You can start with something positive, like great job on this.

115
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:51,560
Then, give suggestions. One thing we could improve is...

116
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:56,060
Let's try it. Great job on the presentation. It was very clear.

117
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:59,260
One thing we could improve is adding more data.

118
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,260
That's constructive and polite.

119
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:06,060
Now, let's do a longer role play using many phrases together.

120
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:08,360
Perfect. Hi, do you have a minute?

121
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,660
Sure. What's up?

122
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,960
I wanted to ask if you could help me with the client presentation.

123
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:15,160
Of course. What do you need help with?

124
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,960
I'm not sure about the structure.

125
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,360
No problem, let's take a look together.

126
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,320
Thanks, I really appreciate it.

127
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:24,840
So, I think we should start with an introduction,

128
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,640
then move to the data.

129
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:27,680
That makes sense.

130
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,800
And maybe we can add a conclusion at the end.

131
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,720
Good idea.

132
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:35,120
Also, we need to finish this by tomorrow, right?

133
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,720
Yes, that's the deadline.

134
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,040
Okay, let's work on it this afternoon.

135
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:39,880
Sounds good.

136
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,240
Thanks again for your help.

137
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,240
Anytime.

138
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,800
That was a great example.

139
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,400
Yes, it shows how natural and simple

140
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:48,320
workplace English can be.

141
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,000
Now let's talk about small talk at work.

142
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,960
Ah yes, casual conversations.

143
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:56,120
You can say, how was your weekend?

144
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,240
Or any plans for today?

145
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,240
Example?

146
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,840
Hey, how was your weekend?

147
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:01,840
It was great.

148
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,280
I relaxed and watched a movie.

149
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,280
What about you?

150
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:07,280
I went for a walk and spent time with family.

151
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,520
Simple and friendly.

152
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:11,800
Now let's talk about ending conversations.

153
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:14,320
You can say, I'll get back to work now.

154
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:16,280
Or let's catch up later.

155
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:22,740
example? Okay, I'll get back to work now. Sure, talk to you later. Perfect. Now, let's

156
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:29,080
do one final full workplace scenario. Great idea. Good morning. How are you? I'm doing

157
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:34,480
well, thank you. How about you? I'm good. Do you have a moment to discuss the project?

158
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:40,200
Yes, of course. I think we need to make some changes to the plan. I see your point. What

159
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:45,360
do you suggest? From my perspective, we should focus more on the client's needs.

160
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,360
That makes sense.

161
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,920
Also, could you update the report?

162
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,920
Sure.

163
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:50,920
I'll do that today.

164
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:51,920
Great.

165
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,440
Let's aim to finish everything by Friday.

166
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,440
Sounds good.

167
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,440
Thanks for your time.

168
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,440
Anytime.

169
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,480
That was a complete workplace conversation.

170
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:03,180
Yes, and you can use these phrases every day.

171
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:06,920
The key is to keep your language simple, polite, and clear.

172
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:07,920
Exactly.

173
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:11,520
You don't need difficult vocabulary to sound professional.

174
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:15,000
Just practice these phrases and use them in real situations.

175
