260
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:06,520
Let's give them some safe and professional phrases.

261
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:09,040
One simple phrase is, I think.

262
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:13,720
Yes, but we can make it more professional by saying, in my opinion.

263
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:16,000
Or from my perspective.

264
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,240
Another useful one is, I believe that.

265
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,200
Let's try a meaning example.

266
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,200
Okay.

267
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:25,340
What do you think about the new marketing strategy?

268
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:29,240
In my opinion, it's a strong idea, but we may need more data.

269
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,320
That's a great response.

270
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,960
Clear and professional.

271
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,920
Now let's talk about agreeing and disagreeing.

272
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:39,880
Yes, this is where communication can become sensitive.

273
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:40,880
Exactly.

274
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,360
You need to be careful and polite.

275
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,200
So how do we agree?

276
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,280
You can say, I agree.

277
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:49,120
Or that makes sense.

278
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,880
Or I completely agree with you.

279
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,080
And what about disagreeing?

280
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:59,240
Instead of saying, you're wrong, you can say, I see your points, but...

281
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,960
That's a great phrase.

282
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:05,120
Another one is, I understand your perspective, however.

283
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,880
Let's try a quick example.

284
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:07,880
Okay.

285
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:10,040
I think we should increase the budget.

286
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:14,560
I see your points, but we need to consider our financial limits.

287
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:15,560
Perfect.

288
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:17,640
That's polite disagreement.

289
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:20,240
Now let's talk about making suggestions.

290
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:23,200
Yes, this is very common in teamwork.

291
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,920
What are some good phrases?

292
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:27,200
You can say, why don't we?

293
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,880
Or how about?

294
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:32,760
Another professional one is, I suggest that we...

295
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:34,240
Let's try an example.

296
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,240
Okay.

297
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,920
We need to improve our customer service.

298
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,000
Any ideas?

299
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,920
I suggest that we provide faster response times.

300
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,760
That's clear and professional.

301
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:47,840
Now let's move to clarifying information.

302
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,760
This is important because misunderstandings happen often.

303
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,760
Exactly.

304
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,920
So what can you say if you don't understand something?

305
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:58,520
You can say, could you clarify that?

306
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:01,080
Or could you explain that again?

307
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:04,860
Another good one is, just to make sure I understand.

308
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:06,400
Let's try an example.

309
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,400
Okay.

310
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:10,600
We need to finalize the report by Friday.

311
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:14,120
Just to make sure I understand, you mean this Friday?

312
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:15,880
Yes, exactly.

313
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:18,000
That's very helpful communication.

314
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,320
Now let's talk about handling problems at work.

315
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,960
This can be stressful, so the language must be careful.

316
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:25,960
Right.

317
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:28,940
Instead of blaming, focus on solutions.

318
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:32,960
So instead of saying, this is your fault, what can we say?

319
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:35,760
You can say, there seems to be an issue.

320
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,400
Or we might have a problem here.

321
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:42,240
Then follow with a solution, let's find a solution.

322
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:43,680
Let's try an example.

323
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:44,680
Okay.

324
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,600
The project is behind schedule.

325
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:48,960
Yes, there seems to be a delay.

326
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:51,360
Let's discuss how we can fix it.

327
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,920
That's very professional.

328
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:57,060
Now let's practice a longer conversation using these phrases.

329
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,060
Great idea!

330
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:00,020
Hi Jack, do you have a moment?

331
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,420
Sure, what's up?

332
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:04,420
I just wanted to ask about the client meeting.

333
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:05,420
Of course!

334
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:06,700
What would you like to know?

335
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,540
Could you clarify the agenda?

336
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:12,100
Yes, we'll discuss the new proposal and the budget.

337
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:13,100
I see.

338
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:16,300
In my opinion, we should focus more on the proposal.

339
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,300
I agree.

340
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,300
That makes sense.

341
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:21,580
Also, I suggest we prepare some examples.

342
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,580
That's a great idea.

343
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:25,580
Thanks. I'd appreciate your help with the slides.

344
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:28,580
Of course. Let's work on them together this afternoon.

345
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:29,580
Perfect.

346
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:32,580
That was a great example of workplace communication.

347
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:36,580
Yes, we used many useful phrases naturally.

348
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:40,580
Exactly. And that's the goal. Sound natural, not robotic.

349
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,580
Now let's do a role play of a team meeting.

350
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:44,580
Perfect.

351
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:47,580
Good morning, everyone. Let's begin the meeting.

352
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:48,580
Good morning.

353
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:49,580
Good morning.

354
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:53,060
Today we're discussing the new project timeline.

355
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:56,120
In my opinion, the timeline is a bit tight.

356
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,620
I see your point.

357
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:58,900
What do you suggest?

358
00:15:58,900 --> 00:16:02,820
I suggest that we extend the deadline by one week.

359
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,980
That makes sense.

360
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,220
Does anyone agree?

361
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:06,220
I agree.

362
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,860
It will give us more time for quality work.

363
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,860
Okay.

364
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:11,340
Let's update the schedule.

365
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:13,500
That was a realistic meeting scenario.

366
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:16,500
Yes, and very useful for learners.

367
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:19,940
Now let's talk about ending conversations politely.

368
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,060
Good point.

369
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:22,860
This is often forgotten.

370
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,140
What can we say?

371
00:16:24,140 --> 00:16:26,580
You can say, thanks for your time.

372
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:28,860
Or I appreciate your help.

373
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:31,620
Another one is, let's follow up later.

374
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:33,100
Let's try an example.

375
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:34,100
Okay.

376
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,540
Thanks for your help today.

377
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:36,540
No problem.

378
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:38,060
Let's follow up tomorrow.

379
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,060
Sounds good.

380
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:41,540
Now let's wrap up everything we learned today.

381
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:43,700
Yes, we covered a lot.

382
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:47,140
We learned how to start conversations professionally.

383
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:49,860
We learned how to ask for help politely.

384
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:52,740
We practiced giving opinions in meetings.

385
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:56,140
We learned how to agree and disagree respectfully.

386
00:16:56,140 --> 00:17:00,580
We talked about making suggestions and clarifying information.

387
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:04,740
And we practiced handling problems and ending conversations.

388
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:09,060
The key is to keep your language simple, clear, and polite.

389
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,060
Exactly.

390
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:13,680
You don't need complicated vocabulary to sound professional.

391
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,160
Just practice these phrases regularly.

392
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,000
Now it's your turn.

393
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:22,680
Today's question is, what phrases do you use at work every day?

394
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:27,000
Write your answer and practice using at least three new phrases from today.

395
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,320
We'd love to read your responses.

396
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,760
Don't worry about mistakes.

397
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,240
That's part of learning.

398
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,440
Absolutely.

399
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,960
Keep practicing and you will improve.

400
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,360
Thank you so much for joining us today.

401
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:42,160
If you enjoyed this lesson, don't forget to like and subscribe.

402
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,380
We'll see you in the next episode.

403
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,880
Take care and keep learning.

404
00:17:45,880 --> 00:17:46,880
Bye, everyone.

405
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:47,880
We're really happy to have you with us today.

406
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,880
Goodbye.

407
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,880
Hi, everyone.

408
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:50,880
Thanks for joining us.

409
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:53,120
If you're here to improve your English for the workplace, you're definitely in the

410
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,120
right place.

411
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:55,120
I'm Emma.

412
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:56,120
And I'm Daniel.

413
00:17:56,120 --> 00:18:00,160
And on this podcast, we help you speak clear, natural English with confidence in real

414
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:02,800
life situations, especially at work.

415
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:06,400
If you enjoy this episode, don't forget to follow us and share it with your friends

416
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,400
or colleagues.

417
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,960
Yes, your support really means a lot to us.

418
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,120
So Emma, what are we talking about today?

419
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:17,320
Today we're diving into a super-practical topic, workplace communication phrases.

420
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,720
That's a big one.

421
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,440
Communication at work is everything, exactly.

422
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:26,200
Whether you're in meetings, writing emails, talking to your boss, or chatting with colleagues,

423
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:29,480
the way you communicate can really shape your success.

424
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,980
And the good news is you don't need perfect English.

425
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:34,840
You just need the right phrases and a bit of confidence.

426
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:35,840
That's right.

427
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:40,400
And today we'll give you tons of practical examples you can start using immediately.

428
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:44,680
You'll also act out real situations so you can hear how native speakers actually talk

429
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:45,680
at work.

430
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:46,680
Sounds great!

431
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,320
So Daniel, how are you feeling today?

432
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:49,480
I'm feeling productive.

433
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:53,520
I had a morning full of meetings, so this topic feels very real right now.

434
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,520
How about you?

435
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:55,520
Same here.

436
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:58,600
I've already used half of the phrases we're going to teach today.

437
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,600
Perfect timing then.

438
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,720
Okay everyone, let's get started.

439
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:04,800
Let's begin with something simple but essential.

440
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,760
Starting a conversation at work.

441
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:07,760
Right.

442
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:10,040
Sometimes the hardest part is just knowing how to begin.

443
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:15,320
Exactly. Imagine you walk into the office or join an online meeting. What do you say?

444
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:20,440
A simple and natural way is, hi, how's it going? Or, good morning, how are things?

445
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:24,200
You can also be a bit more specific, like, how's your day going so far?

446
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:27,160
That sounds friendly and professional at the same time.

447
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:31,560
Yes, and if you want to move into work quickly, you can say, shall we get started?

448
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:35,240
Or, let's jump right in. I use that one a lot in meetings.

449
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,040
Me too. Okay, let's do a quick example.

450
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,840
Sure. Hi Daniel, how's your day going so far?

451
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:43,720
Pretty good, thanks. Just finished a report. How about you?

452
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,200
Not bad. Shall we get started with the meeting?

453
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:49,960
Yes, let's do it. See? Very simple, but very natural.

454
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:53,640
Exactly. Now let's talk about asking for help at work.

455
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:58,200
This is something everyone needs to do, but many learners feel nervous about it.

456
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:01,160
Right. You don't want to sound too direct or rude.

457
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:04,120
So instead of saying help me, you can say,

458
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:08,200
Could you help me with this or would you mind taking a look at this?

459
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,280
That's a great one. Very polite.

460
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:13,800
Another useful phrase is, I'd really appreciate your input.

461
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,040
That sounds professional and respectful.

462
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,480
Let's try a situation.

463
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,360
Speaker 1.

464
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:21,080
Hey Daniel, could you help me with this presentation?

465
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:21,880
Speaker 2.

466
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,720
Of course. What do you need help with?

467
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,760
Speaker 1.

468
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:27,480
I'd really appreciate your input on the design.

469
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,280
Speaker 2.

470
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:29,640
Sure. Let me take a look.

471
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,680
Perfect.

472
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:33,160
Now let's talk about giving opinions.

473
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,560
This is especially important in meetings.

474
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:39,120
Yes, and it's important to sound confident but polite.

475
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:43,080
A simple way to start is I think, or in my opinion.

476
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,480
If you want to sound a bit softer, you can say,

477
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:48,600
I feel that, or it seems to me that.

478
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,400
And if you want to be very professional,

479
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,440
try from my perspective.

480
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,000
That's a strong phrase.

481
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,040
Let's practice.

482
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,240
Speaker one, from my perspective,

483
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,840
we should focus more on customer feedback.

484
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:01,760
Speaker two, that's a good point.

485
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,980
I think it could really improve our product.

486
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:05,000
Nice.

487
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,300
Now what about agreeing with someone?

488
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:08,760
Ah, very important.

489
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,240
You want to show your listening.

490
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:13,520
You can say, I agree, or that makes sense.

491
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:16,180
Another great one is I couldn't agree more.

492
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:17,980
Yes, that's very natural.

493
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,900
Let's try it.

494
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:22,020
Speaker two, I think we should extend the deadline.

495
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:24,440
Speaker one, I couldn't agree more.

496
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,860
It would give us more time to improve the quality.

497
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:27,700
Excellent.

498
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,960
Now let's talk about disagreeing.

499
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,220
This can be tricky.

500
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:33,100
You don't want to sound rude.

501
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,100
Exactly.

502
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:36,020
So instead of saying, you're wrong,

503
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:37,860
you can say, I see your point,

504
00:21:37,860 --> 00:21:40,420
but that's a very useful phrase.

505
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:43,420
Or I understand what you're saying, however.

506
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:46,980
Another option is, I'm not sure I completely agree.

507
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:48,300
Let's try a role play.

508
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,300
Speaker one.

509
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:51,900
I think we should launch the product next week.

510
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,940
Speaker two, I see your point,

511
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:56,300
but I think we need more testing first.

512
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,300
That sounds polite and professional.

513
00:21:58,300 --> 00:21:59,260
Exactly.

514
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:01,260
Now let's move into a longer role play,

515
00:22:01,260 --> 00:22:03,580
where we use many of these phrases together.

516
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:06,380
Great idea, let's imagine a team meeting.

517
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:09,380
Speaker one, good morning everyone, thanks for joining.

518
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:12,140
Speaker two, good morning, shall we get started?

519
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:15,500
Yes, the first item on the agenda is the new project.

520
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,820
Speaker one, from my perspective,

521
00:22:17,820 --> 00:22:20,760
we should focus on improving customer experience.

522
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:23,980
Speaker two, I agree, that's very important.

523
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:25,580
Speaker two, however,

524
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,180
I think we also need to consider the budget.

525
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,200
Speaker 1. That makes sense.

526
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:33,520
Speaker 2. Could you help me analyze the costs?

527
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:36,120
Speaker 1. Of course, I'd be happy to help.

528
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:39,520
Speaker 2. Great. Let's move on to the timeline.

529
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:42,020
